{"title":"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Closely-related_question_and_solution_(podcast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Closely-related question and solution (podcast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many three-digit numbers are composed of three distinct digits such that one digit is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Average\" title=\"Average\">average</a> of the other two? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/f/f0f2d5df8de2487beedbcd854b3081b71fb3b03b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 96\\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ 104\\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 112\\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 120\\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ 256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"423\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can find the number of increasing <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic_sequence\" title=\"Arithmetic sequence\">arithmetic sequences</a> of length 3 possible from 0 to 9, and then find all the possible permutations of these sequences.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" border=\"1px solid\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Common difference</td>\n<td>Sequences possible</td>\n<td>Number of sequences\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bb3f469084a2f441ddf2ce046453dc12f458e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$012, \\ldots, 789$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /></td>\n<td>8\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/5/3654646e478d720bd2538a4ddc0475c84792c088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$024, \\ldots, 579$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /></td>\n<td>6\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/3/3936532990c2b273ed3a08db19b9fa5e1dde77e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$036, \\ldots, 369$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /></td>\n<td>4\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3f78c70f027ae1dd3f1d2caf438550702955046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$048, \\ldots, 159$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /></td>\n<td>2\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>This gives us a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae64dd900275f0e6db4764851eb16499071ccc87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 4 + 6 + 8 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" /> sequences. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db3b59940e4f5cd42bbab2b7815c452a0197507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3! = 6$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> to permute these, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>However, we note that the conditions of the problem require three-digit numbers, and hence our numbers cannot start with zero. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/5/715f3e84a4f9ca515bb0946d5db287f373d25959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2! \\cdot 4 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> numbers which start with zero, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b7dac6629488f80ac80e000b4f0c50553e5c2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120 - 8 = 112 \\Longrightarrow \\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that, if the smallest and largest digit have the same parity, this uniquely determines the middle digit. If the smallest digit is not zero, then any choice of the smallest and largest digit gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db3b59940e4f5cd42bbab2b7815c452a0197507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3! = 6$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> possible 3-digit numbers; otherwise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible 3-digit numbers. Hence we can do simple casework on whether 0 is in the number or not.\n</p><p>Case 1: 0 is not in the number. Then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab87b3885ddeede48365048af2e36b9c6939fdf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{5}{2} + \\binom{4}{2} = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"141\" height=\"55\" /> ways to choose two nonzero digits of the same parity, and each choice generates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db3b59940e4f5cd42bbab2b7815c452a0197507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3! = 6$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> 3-digit numbers, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9af853a4be65e2af2ef07cf60107b741157e629.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\times 6 = 96$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> numbers.\n</p><p>Case 2: 0 is in the number. Then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose the largest digit (2, 4, 6, or 8), and each choice generates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> 3-digit numbers, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/541f4f0ac5c46d4e572ab6d69e704f8ad1810583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 4 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> numbers.\n</p><p>Thus the total is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/090df3c982f5350cecb3a07acfb2d999bda649fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$96 + 16 = 112 \\Longrightarrow \\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />. (by scrabbler94)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0W3VmFp55cM?t=2012\">https://youtu.be/0W3VmFp55cM?t=2012</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Closely-related_question_and_solution_.28podcast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Closely-related_question_and_solution_(podcast)\">Closely-related question and solution (podcast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Closely-related question and solution (podcast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.buzzsprout.com/56982/episodes/415913\">https://www.buzzsprout.com/56982/episodes/415913</a> starts with a variation on this question (plus solution)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">similar problem in 2005</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A\">2007 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a h